    "scenario": "BGP Local Preference MED",
    "goals": "• Configure IBGP within AS100, the source of BGP updates has to be the loopback interface.\n  AS100: {{router1_name}}, {{router2_name}}, {{router4_name}}\n• Configure EBGP between router {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}}.\n  {{router3_name}} is in AS200.\n• Configure EBGP between router {{router1_name}} and {{router3_name}}.\n  {{router3_name}} is in AS200.\n• Advertise the loopback interfaces into BGP, do this on all routers.\n• Ensure you have full reachability to all loopback networks.\n• You need to make sure that all traffic for AS100 is being sent using the link between router {{router1_name}} and {{router3_name}}. You are only allowed to make changes on router {{router1_name}} or {{router2_name}}. (hint: use MED)\n• To conform to the company policy, you need to make sure that all outgoing traffic will be sent using the link between router {{router1_name}} and {{router3_name}}. (hint: use Local Preference)",
